ini|zucchini]] (courgette), chopped\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomato]], chopped\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]], chopped\n* 1 tablespoon [[Cookbook:Flour|flour]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* ½ teaspoon powdered [[Cookbook:Paprika|paprika]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Pinch|pinch]] ground [[Cookbook:Clove|cloves]]\n* 1 pinch ground [[Cookbook:Pepper|pepper]]\n* 6–8 [[Cookbook:Coriander|coriander]] seeds\n* [[Cookbook:Oil and Fat|Oil]]\n\n==Procedure==\n# Roll the placenta in a mix of the flour, salt, paprika, clove, pepper, and 6-8 coriander seeds.\n# [[Cookbook:Sautéing|Sauté]] the placenta in 2 tablespoons oil, then add the vegetables and about 1 [[Cookbook:Liter|litre]] of water.\n# Allow to boil, and then let simmer for an hour.\n\n==Warnings==\n\n* As with any meat from uncontrolled sources (such as hunting or scavenging) people should be cautious of risks involved. Certain blood borne diseases can live in blood and tissue outside the body for some time. Be sure that sensible precautions have been taken.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using placenta]]\n[[Category:Recipes for stew]]\n[[Category:Recipes using carrot]]\n[[Category:Recipes using celery]]\n[[Category:Recipes using clove]]\n[[Category:Recipes using coriander]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Placenta Stew","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"¾ fresh human placenta","sourceText":"¾ fresh human placenta","amountText":"¾ fresh human placenta","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 potato, diced","sourceText":"1 potato, diced","amountText":"1 potato, diced","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"4 tablespoons fresh parsley","sourceText":"4 tablespoons fresh parsley","amountText":"4 tablespoons fresh parsley","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"2 carrots, chopped","sourceText":"2